# Shell scripts must keep LF endings even when checked out on Windows.
# With core.autocrlf=true git rewrites them to CRLF, and bash then fails on
# the trailing \r -- either "bad interpreter" on the shebang, or subtler:
# a URL captured from command substitution ends in \r and every request
# becomes https://host%0D/path, which 404s at Google's frontend.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf

# Binary. Without this git applies CRLF conversion on checkout and silently
# corrupts them -- a PDF that opens fine here and is unreadable after a clone.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.drawio binary
